# Library Management System - Walkthrough

## What Was Built
I have successfully implemented a full-stack locally running Library Management System.
- **Backend**: Built with Java 17 and Spring Boot (Spring MVC, Spring Data JPA).
- **Database**: H2 in-memory database configuration ensures a zero-friction start without needing external MySQL/PostgreSQL servers.
- **Frontend**: A custom React application embedded directly into the Spring Boot backend ([src/main/resources/static/app.js](file:///c:/Users/ayush/OneDrive%20-%20Noida%20International%20University/Desktop/library%20project/backend/src/main/resources/static/app.js)). This allowed you to quickly test it without needing to install Node.js!
- **Design Aesthetic**: Premium glassmorphism design using seamless CSS. 

## Workflow Features
- **Dashboard Overview**: See top-level metrics quickly.
- **Book Management**: Full CRUD capabilities for library books.
- **Member Management**: Track active members.
- **Borrowing Engine**: Check out available books and log them against active members.

## Validation & Proof of Work
The backend was successfully built via Maven and started on port `8080`.
The browser automation agent performed a complete End-to-End flow:
1. Created "The Great Gatsby" book.
2. Created "John Doe" member.
3. Successfully checked the book out to the member.

